Q: Weird IllegalArgumentException - Spring 6.1 cannot find controller method parameters despite -parameters being passed in compiler A: <p>I think, you are falling victim to <a href="https://bugs.openjdk.org/browse/JDK-8240908" rel="nofollow noreferrer">JDK-8240908</a>, a problem in Java instrumentation: Any transformer (e.g. DataDog agent) using <a href="https://docs.oracle.com/en/java/javase/17/docs/api/java.instrument/java/lang/instrument/Instrumentation.html#retransformClasses(java.lang.Class...)" rel="nofollow noreferrer"><code>Instrumentation.retransformClasses</code></a> will make the resulting class lose method parameter information. This was fixed in JDK 19, which is why currently there is <a href="https://github.com/DataDog/dd-trace-java/pull/10521" rel="nofollow noreferrer">DataDog PR 10521</a> to make DataDog skip transformation in affected cases on JDKs less than 19.</p>
<p>Interestingly, on the old JDK ticket there has been <a href="https://bugs.openjdk.org/browse/JDK-8240908?focusedId=14853823&amp;page=com.atlassian.jira.plugin.system.issuetabpanels%3Acomment-tabpanel#comment-14853823" rel="nofollow noreferrer">recent activity</a> for a JDK 17 backport, corresponding <a href="https://github.com/openjdk/jdk17u-dev/pull/4265" rel="nofollow noreferrer">
OpenJDK PR 4265</a> has already been opened. So, in the future DataDog and other affected java agents might be able to securely use retransformation again on JDK 17, if the update used is at least the version containing the backported fix from the PR.</p>
<p>Your current option to avoid the problem is to talk to operations in your company and find out if they could upgrade the Java runtime on the affected systems to at least 19, probably rather LTS 21.</p>
<h3>JDK-8240908 reproducer</h3>
<pre class="lang-xml prettyprint-override"><code>&lt;?xml version=&quot;1.0&quot; encoding=&quot;UTF-8&quot;?&gt;
&lt;project xmlns=&quot;http://maven.apache.org/POM/4.0.0&quot; xmlns:xsi=&quot;http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema-instance&quot;
  xsi:schemaLocation=&quot;http://maven.apache.org/POM/4.0.0 http://maven.apache.org/xsd/maven-4.0.0.xsd&quot;&gt;
  &lt;modelVersion&gt;4.0.0&lt;/modelVersion&gt;

  &lt;groupId&gt;de.scrum-master&lt;/groupId&gt;
  &lt;artifactId&gt;jdk-8240908-reproducer&lt;/artifactId&gt;
  &lt;version&gt;1.0-SNAPSHOT&lt;/version&gt;
  &lt;name&gt;JDK-8240908 reproducer&lt;/name&gt;

  &lt;properties&gt;
    &lt;maven.compiler.source&gt;11&lt;/maven.compiler.source&gt;
    &lt;maven.compiler.target&gt;11&lt;/maven.compiler.target&gt;
    &lt;project.build.sourceEncoding&gt;UTF-8&lt;/project.build.sourceEncoding&gt;
    &lt;byte-buddy.version&gt;1.15.1&lt;/byte-buddy.version&gt;
  &lt;/properties&gt;

  &lt;dependencies&gt;
    &lt;dependency&gt;
      &lt;groupId&gt;net.bytebuddy&lt;/groupId&gt;
      &lt;artifactId&gt;byte-buddy-agent&lt;/artifactId&gt;
      &lt;version&gt;${byte-buddy.version}&lt;/version&gt;
    &lt;/dependency&gt;
  &lt;/dependencies&gt;

  &lt;build&gt;
    &lt;plugins&gt;
      &lt;plugin&gt;
        &lt;groupId&gt;org.apache.maven.plugins&lt;/groupId&gt;
        &lt;artifactId&gt;maven-compiler-plugin&lt;/artifactId&gt;
        &lt;version&gt;3.13.0&lt;/version&gt;
        &lt;configuration&gt;
          &lt;source&gt;11&lt;/source&gt;
          &lt;target&gt;11&lt;/target&gt;
          &lt;parameters&gt;true&lt;/parameters&gt;
        &lt;/configuration&gt;
      &lt;/plugin&gt;
    &lt;/plugins&gt;
  &lt;/build&gt;
&lt;/project&gt;
</code></pre>
<pre class="lang-java prettyprint-override"><code>package de.scrum_master;

public class Target {
  public void doSomething(String text, int number) {}
}
</code></pre>
<pre class="lang-java prettyprint-override"><code>package de.scrum_master;

import net.bytebuddy.agent.ByteBuddyAgent;

import java.lang.instrument.Instrumentation;
import java.lang.instrument.UnmodifiableClassException;
import java.lang.reflect.Method;
import java.lang.reflect.Parameter;
import java.util.stream.Collectors;

import static java.util.Arrays.stream;

public class Main {
  private static final Instrumentation INSTRUMENTATION = ByteBuddyAgent.install();

  public static void main(String[] args) throws UnmodifiableClassException {
    System.out.println(&quot;=== BEFORE RETRANSFORMATION ===&quot;);
    printParameterNames(Target.class);
    INSTRUMENTATION.retransformClasses(Target.class);
    System.out.println(&quot;=== AFTER RETRANSFORMATION (JDK &lt; 19 should lose param names) ===&quot;);
    // On JDK &lt; 19, prints &quot;doSomething(arg0, arg1)&quot; instead of &quot;doSomething(text, number)&quot;
    printParameterNames(Target.class);
  }

  public static void printParameterNames(Class&lt;?&gt; clazz) {
    for (Method method : clazz.getDeclaredMethods()) {
      String paramNames = stream(method.getParameters()).map(Parameter::getName).collect(Collectors.joining(&quot;, &quot;));
      System.out.println(method.getName() + &quot;(&quot; + paramNames + &quot;)&quot;);
    }
  }
}
</code></pre>
<p>Just run the main class from the console or your IDE of choice, e.g. on JDK 18- to reproduce the problem and on JDK 19+ to see that is was fixed. I tried with JDKs 11, 17, 19, 21, 24 and could clearly see the difference.</p>

